{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T01:21:07-07:00","id":1317523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317522#post1317522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft: Genesis isn't a thing anymore - you accomplish the same effect via Workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're kinda of a downer, man. <br /> <br /> That was a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T01:33:16-07:00","id":1317525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317523#post1317523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes, Exalted genius crafters should specialize in creating magical science projects by having sex with them, har, har. I don't particularly find that funny or compelling considering how a number of people have been suggesting it completely straight-faced for years now. Particularly as regards female characters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T02:08:51-07:00","id":1317528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317525#post1317525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes, Exalted genius crafters should specialize in creating magical science projects by having sex with them, har, har. I don't particularly find that funny or compelling considering how a number of people have been suggesting it completely straight-faced for years now. Particularly as regards female characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever. I'm too tired.<br /> <br /> Just go somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T03:50:28-07:00","id":1317538,"title":"","content":"Let me dredge some up from my NPC character sheets:<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy:<br /> - Anticorruption<br /> - Customs<br /> - Finance<br /> - Shipping<br /> - Satrapial Governance<br /> <br /> Investigation:<br /> - Anticorruption<br /> - Finance<br /> - Smuggling<br /> <br /> Larceny:<br /> - Diguise<br /> - Embezzlement<br /> <br /> Lore:<br /> - Blessed Isle Trade<br /> - Dynastic Commerce<br /> - Dynastic Politics<br /> - Exalts<br /> - Spirits<br /> <br /> Socialise:<br /> - Galas<br /> - Imperial Service<br /> <br /> War:<br /> - Recruitment<br /> - Strategic Planning<br /> <br /> Loosely classified as either a specialty in a particular context, or a specialty in a particular action (eg: You might be good at all applications of Investigation in a smuggling context but only have a specialty for Case Scenes outside of that.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24811-grelkis","name":"Grelkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T04:09:13-07:00","id":1317541,"title":"","content":"War:<br /> <br /> Training<br /> Special Ops<br /> Defensive<br /> Siege breaking <br /> <br /> Craft (genesis)<br /> Genetic alteration <br /> Human augmentation <br /> Crop engineering<br /> Artificial organs<br /> <br /> Craft (technology)<br /> Computers<br /> Aerospace engineering <br /> Firearms<br /> Factories <br /> Programming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T05:35:53-07:00","id":1317545,"title":"","content":"What is your definition of techonology? Swords and spinning wheels are &quot;technology&quot; too, and even in a setting which allows modern day electronic and mechanical items...<br /> <br /> There is no way a &quot;Craft: Technology&quot; allowing you to make both laptops and shotguns could exist. They are both different abilities, Craft: Electronic Engineering and Craft: Gunsmithing. It\u00b4s like having &quot;Craft: Old Things&quot; allowing you to make swords, glass, a linen dress and a wooden ship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T07:44:10-07:00","id":1317563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317505#post1317505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We mustn't forget the nearly all purpose &quot;While nude.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In the very first game of Exalted I ever ran, one character was a Zenith who had Melee, Resistance and Survival specialties in &quot;While nude&quot;. He had a custom charm for reflexively whipping off his clothes if a fight broke out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T07:53:33-07:00","id":1317565,"title":"","content":"Let's have a look...<br /> <br /> My Zenith has Integrity (vs Spirits); Investigation (Murders); Medicine (Autopsy); Occult (Ghosts); Performance (Prayers); Presence (vs Spirits).<br /> <br /> My snake totem kung-fu doctor just has Resistance (Poison), Medicine (Poison) and Martial Arts (Unarmed). Not that exciting I guess.<br /> <br /> My old character, an Owl-totem sorcerer, had Integrity (vs Fae), Stealth (In Darkness) and Survival (Hunting).<br /> Fae were always messing with him because he broke up with his evil twin's Raksha girlfriend (they'd both thought he was the evil twin, it's a long story), and she told all her family to punish him. So they'd try and get him into trouble, impersonate the guy he was in love with, that kind of thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T07:57:26-07:00","id":1317567,"title":"","content":"Some of the more interesting specialties the players in my Lunar game have: Athletics (Flee!), Sail (Longboats), Performance (Acting Cute) and Presence (Inflicting fear) (on the same character!), Athletics (Brachiation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T08:18:18-07:00","id":1317570,"title":"","content":"For Knight Raiton I've got:<br /> \u200bDodge (Multiple Opponents)<br /> Presence (Intimidation)<br /> Stealth (Cities)<br /> Thrown (Boomerangs)<br /> <br /> \u200bFor his rich playboy persona, Carter Brus, I've got:<br /> Presence (Charm)<br /> Bureaucracy (Negotiation)<br /> Socialize (Parties)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T08:31:10-07:00","id":1317583,"title":"","content":"My last character, a Dawn Caste girl who Exalted when a pirate burned her town and she miraculously survived, and had... some understandable rage issues, had the specialty Brawl (Cute Little Ball of Hatred)<br /> <br /> Basically, the specialty applied whenever she had a Hate-based intimacy towards an enemy, or if the target had enraged her in any way (acting publicly against her intimacies, being a pirate or serving fae. The pirate captain who killed her father was Fae-Blooded and in her mind, Fae=Evil).<br /> <br /> She also had Craft:Cooking (Cakes and desserts) and Bureaucracy: Accounting. She was the eldest daughter of a widower innkeeper, and was going to take over the family business once she grew up, so she had some training with numbers (only one Bureaucracy dot, she was like thirteen or so, but it\u00b4s something!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T09:09:21-07:00","id":1317593,"title":"","content":"One of the characters in my 2nd ed game had Craft Water (Tea) and the charm that gave extra successes to Craft Water.<br /> <br /> So he'd brew up the most amazing teas in the world basically every night for the party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T09:32:53-07:00","id":1317597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317541#post1317541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War:<br /> <br /> Training<br /> Special Ops<br /> Defensive<br /> Siege breaking<br /> <br /> Craft (genesis)<br /> Genetic alteration<br /> Human augmentation<br /> Crop engineering<br /> Artificial organs<br /> <br /> Craft (technology)<br /> Computers<br /> Aerospace engineering<br /> Firearms<br /> Factories<br /> Programming</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you not venturing into the realms of Medicine with those craft specialties of yours ? A prosthetic would surely be Craft, sure, but an organ? I find that many of your specialities smell a bit like Magi-tech, which is no longer a thing in 3ed as far as I understand. Note, this is just my impression, I am not saying you are wrong with your specialities, I just would never use most of them in my own game as a GM in 3ed, and agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> that you are venturing into the territory of Sorcerous Workings with some of those specialties (as well as Medicine as previously stated).<br /> Otherwise, I like your specialties, but as stated, I am not a fan of the Craft Specialties you listed personally.<br /> <br /> Some of my more mundane ideas:<br /> <br /> Craft:<br /> Woodworking (one of my players have toy-making as a specialty for this craft)<br /> Leatherworking<br /> Ship Building<br /> Architecture<br /> Engineering (maybe this is too broad, not sure really, though I have it on a character that where I play as a twilight sorcerer-engineer in a campaign a friend of mine is running)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24253,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","user":"Magnus K","date":". 06-10-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T09:42:56-07:00","id":1317601,"title":"","content":"Craft (Genesis) is a 2nd ed thing anyway (it doesn't exist in 3rd ed), so it doesn't really matter if Craft (Genesis) specialties look like magitech.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T10:09:43-07:00","id":1317612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317597#post1317597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you not venturing into the realms of Medicine with those craft specialties of yours ? A prosthetic would surely be Craft, sure, but an organ? I find that many of your specialities smell a bit like Magi-tech, which is no longer a thing in 3ed as far as I understand. Note, this is just my impression, I am not saying you are wrong with your specialities, I just would never use most of them in my own game as a GM in 3ed, and agree with <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> that you are venturing into the territory of Sorcerous Workings with some of those specialties (as well as Medicine as previously stated).<br /> Otherwise, I like your specialties, but as stated, I am not a fan of the Craft Specialties you listed personally.<br /> <br /> Some of my more mundane ideas:<br /> <br /> Craft:<br /> Woodworking (one of my players have toy-making as a specialty for this craft)<br /> Leatherworking<br /> Ship Building<br /> Architecture<br /> Engineering (maybe this is too broad, not sure really, though I have it on a character that where I play as a twilight sorcerer-engineer in a campaign a friend of mine is running)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <br /> <br /> I'm currently learning biotech right now. And those are fields that I'm kinda hoping to touch on later in my life.<br /> <br /> So what's the line between craft and medicine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T10:18:39-07:00","id":1317616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317612#post1317612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> I'm currently learning biotech right now. And those are fields that I'm kinda hoping to touch on later in my life.<br /> <br /> So what's the line between craft and medicine?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there are 100% clear lines always in Exalted. I just associated those Craft specialties more with other abilities, such as medicine (because medicine surely involves surgery and more advanced surgery). I think, sometimes a GMs, we just have to use common sense, for lack of better word. I am not saying you are wrong, I am just saying that personally, as a GM, I would associate for instance Genetic Alteration and artifical organs with Medicine and not Craft, so for me, those very specialised specialties would be medicine in my games. But if you are a GM, then you may rule otherwise yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T10:31:42-07:00","id":1317618,"title":"","content":"Considering you only have to buy Medicine once, and Craft seperately, I'd be inclined to just have all medical-making stuff be Medicine.<br /> <br /> But my ST had me buy Craft (Pharmacology) for making medicine and drugs and poisons and stuff. Which is okay (the character is a Lunar, not a Solar, so she can use Intelligence charms for both, not just Medicine charms on Medicine and Craft charms on Craft. I have a charm that gives me Craft points for doing medicine with stuff I made anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T15:24:45-07:00","id":1317691,"title":"","content":"I like using specialties as little bits of character flavour. Examples include:<ul><li>Athletics (Natural Dancer)</li> <li>Craft (Exotic and <i>Wrong)</i></li> <li>Dodge (Small)</li> <li>Integrity (Indignation)</li> <li>Investigation (Tactile)</li> <li>Melee (For Justice); Melee (Mystical Circumstances)</li> <li>Performance (Voice of an Earth God)</li> <li>Presence (Appeasing the Dead)</li> <li>Resistance (Ritual Purity); Resistance (Self-Sacrifice)</li> <li>Socialize (Inscrutable Smile)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T16:27:19-07:00","id":1317698,"title":"","content":"My group loves to get Overly-Specific Specializations. Some of the PCs specialties include :<ul><li>Awareness (the sound of paper that is unfolding)</li> <li>Survival (Mountain Agriculture)</li> <li>Socialize (Hiding the fact that you have a cold)</li> <li>Presence (Interacting with people who aren't real)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T17:41:48-07:00","id":1317709,"title":"","content":"Craft:<br /> Reverse engineering<br /> Designing new things<br /> Poor conditions<br /> Mass production<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy: <br /> Increasing efficiency<br /> Upgrading systems<br /> Purging corrupt<br /> Distributing goods<br /> Transportation networks<br /> Human resources<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T17:50:29-07:00","id":1317710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317563#post1317563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the very first game of Exalted I ever ran, one character was a Zenith who had Melee, Resistance and Survival specialties in &quot;While nude&quot;. He had a custom charm for reflexively whipping off his clothes if a fight broke out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm I may use this. <br /> <br /> Oh since I'm helping one of my players figure out their war specialty.<br /> War:<br /> Supplies<br /> Requisition<br /> Delegation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T18:24:36-07:00","id":1317716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317710#post1317710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm I may use this.<br /> <br /> Oh since I'm helping one of my players figure out their war specialty.<br /> War:<br /> Supplies<br /> Requisition<br /> <b>Delegation</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm....<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy:<br /> Finding talented people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T14:14:20-07:00","id":1317871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1317471-thinking-up-specialties?p=1317525#post1317525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes, Exalted genius crafters should specialize in creating magical science projects by having sex with them, har, har. I don't particularly find that funny or compelling considering how a number of people have been suggesting it completely straight-faced for years now. Particularly as regards female characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The joke was that Craft: Genesis can be a euphemism for procreation, not..Whatever you're thinking here.<br /> <br /> Movin' on!<br /> <br /> Resistance: Sleep deprivation<br /> <br /> Lore: Laws of Nexus (for actually knowing them)<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy: Laws of Nexus (for navigating and exploiting them)<br /> <br /> Presence: Laws of Nexus (for realizing that apart from the big five, you can convince anyone that anything is illegal in Nexus with enough confidence.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T14:22:29-07:00","id":1317874,"title":"","content":"Or legal, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"a